('GPU — Graphics Processing Unit','stack','A processor designed to perform many calculations in parallel. GPUs accelerate AI training, inference and other compute-intensive workloads.','','GPUs accelerator','gpu'),
('GPU cluster','stack','A connected group of GPU servers that can run coordinated workloads. Cluster performance depends on compute, networking, storage and software working together.','','clusters','factory'),
('GPU usage / consumption','operational-value','The amount of GPU resource used or allocated over a period, often measured in GPU-hours. Specify whether the figure means allocated time, billed consumption or active computation.','Eight GPUs allocated for ten hours equal 80 allocated GPU-hours, even if the workload leaves them idle part of the time.','GPU consumption GPU use','editorial'),
('GPU-hour','business-value','One GPU allocated or used for one hour, under a stated measurement or billing definition. GPU model, service configuration and billing terms must be comparable when discussing price per GPU-hour.','','GPU hours GPU-hours','editorial'),
('GPU utilization','operational-value','A measure of GPU activity over time. NVIDIA’s common utilization metric reports the share of sampled time with a GPU kernel running; a high reading alone does not prove useful work or peak efficiency.','A GPU can be allocated to a paying customer all day while spending part of that day waiting for data.','GPU utilisation','utilization'),
('GPU memory utilization','technical-value','A GPU memory metric whose meaning depends on the tool: it may describe memory activity or the share of memory capacity occupied. State the metric explicitly; neither is the same as compute utilization.','','VRAM memory usage','utilization'),
('GPU capacity occupancy','business-value','The share of a provider’s available GPU capacity allocated or committed to customers over a defined period. This commercial measure is separate from GPU compute utilization and CUDA SM occupancy.','If 80 of 100 comparable GPUs are customer-allocated for the same period, allocation-based capacity occupancy is 80%.','commercial utilization commercial utilisation sold capacity','editorial'),
('GPU starvation','pain','A situation in which GPUs wait for input data instead of progressing the workload. Storage, networking or data preparation may cause the delay; the bottleneck needs measurement.','','data starvation GPU idle idle GPUs','certification'),
('AI training','use-case','The process of learning model parameters from data. Infrastructure needs depend on the model, dataset, training method and scale.','','model training pretraining pre-training','training'),
('Fine-tuning','use-case','Additional training of an existing model on selected data to adapt it to a task, domain or behavior. It changes model parameters.','','fine tuning finetuning','training'),
('Inference','use-case','Running a trained model on new inputs to produce outputs, such as answers, predictions or generated content.','','inferencing model serving','inference'),
('LLM — Large Language Model','use-case','An AI model trained on large amounts of data to understand and generate language. Its size and usage pattern affect memory, compute and data requirements.','','LLMs language models','training'),
('RAG — Retrieval-Augmented Generation','use-case','Retrieving relevant information and supplying it to a generative model as context for an answer. RAG can use current enterprise information without retraining the model for every document update.','An assistant retrieves approved product documentation before answering a customer’s configuration question.','retrieval augmented generation','rag'),
('Token','use-case','A unit of content processed by an AI model, such as a word fragment or punctuation mark in text. Token counts depend on the model’s tokenizer; one token is not always one word.','','tokens tokenization','inference'),
('Tokens per second','operational-value','The rate at which a model or service processes or generates tokens. State whether it is input or output throughput and whether the measurement is per user, per GPU or across the service.','','TPS token throughput','inference'),
('TTFT — Time to First Token','operational-value','The time from submitting a request until the first output token arrives. It describes the initial wait, not the time needed to finish the response.','','time-to-first-token','inference'),
('Cost per token','business-value','The cost of processing or generating tokens under a defined workload and cost scope, often expressed per million tokens. Provider delivery cost and the customer’s billed price are different measures.','','cost per million tokens inference economics','economics'),
('Checkpointing','technical-value','Saving training state so a job can resume after an interruption. Checkpoint size, write time and restore time affect storage requirements and productive training time.','','checkpoint checkpoints','checkpoint'),
