('Infinia','technical-value','DDN’s software-defined data platform with multi-tenancy, metadata capabilities and multi-protocol access. It supports data-intensive workflows including AI data preparation, analytics and inference.','','DDN Infinia','infinia'),
('Lustre','technical-value','An open-source parallel file system designed for large-scale, high-performance computing. DDN EXAScaler builds on Lustre.','','Lustre file system','lustre'),
('Parallel file system','technical-value','A file system that distributes data and I/O across multiple storage resources so many clients can access shared data concurrently at scale.','','parallel filesystem','lustre'),
('Object storage','technical-value','Storage that organizes data as objects with identifiers and metadata, typically accessed through an API. It differs from accessing files through a mounted directory hierarchy.','','object store','storage'),
('File storage','technical-value','Storage accessed as named files in directories through a file system. Applications use file operations to open, read, write and manage data.','','file system filesystem','storage'),
('S3-compatible','technical-value','Supporting Amazon S3-style APIs for object access. Compatibility does not mean the service runs on AWS or supports every S3 feature.','','S3 S3 compatible','storage'),
('Throughput','technical-value','The amount of data successfully transferred per unit of time, often MB/s or GB/s. Sustained workload throughput can differ from a component’s advertised maximum.','','bandwidth GB/s TB/s','storage'),
('Latency','technical-value','The time taken to complete a defined operation or return a response. State the operation and measurement, such as average or 99th-percentile read latency.','','response time p99','storage'),
('IOPS — Input/Output Operations per Second','technical-value','The number of storage read or write operations completed each second. Interpret IOPS alongside operation size, access pattern and latency.','','I/O operations','storage'),
('Metadata','technical-value','Information describing data, such as its name, size, owner, timestamps or tags. Metadata performance matters when applications discover or manage large numbers of files or objects.','','metadata operations','infinia'),
('Usable capacity','technical-value','Storage capacity available for customer data after protection and system overheads. Raw drive capacity and usable capacity are different numbers.','','raw capacity','editorial'),
('Data locality','technical-value','How close data is to the compute that uses it, physically or logically. Placement affects transfer time, network traffic and the need to copy datasets.','','data placement','editorial'),
('Reference architecture','technical-value','A documented design showing how components should work together for a use case. Alignment to a reference architecture does not by itself prove certification or the customer’s measured performance.','','RA validated design','ncp'),
('NVIDIA-Certified Storage','nvidia','NVIDIA’s program for validating storage against specified AI infrastructure requirements. Certification applies to the tested product and configuration scope, not automatically to every offering from a vendor.','','NVIDIA certification certified storage','certification'),
('QoS — Quality of Service','technical-value','Controls or service targets that govern how resources and performance are shared. QoS helps prevent one tenant or workload from overwhelming others.','','quality of service noisy neighbor noisy neighbour','tenancy'),
('SLA — Service-Level Agreement','paper-process','An agreement defining service commitments, how they are measured and what happens if they are missed. Availability, performance and support response commitments should be read in their specific contract context.','','service level agreement SLAs','editorial'),
('TCO — Total Cost of Ownership','business-value','The full cost of acquiring and operating a solution over a stated period, including relevant hardware, software, support, staffing, power and facilities costs.','','total cost ownership','editorial'),
('ROI — Return on Investment','business-value','Net benefit divided by investment cost over a defined period, usually expressed as a percentage. Use a consistent cost basis and customer-validated benefit assumptions.','With $150,000 in benefits and $100,000 in total investment costs over the same period, ROI is 50%.','return on investment','editorial'),
